WEBVTT

00:00:00.550 --> 00:00:05.069
Inside a developing zebrafish, the heart contracts and blood

00:00:05.069 --> 00:00:09.587
circulates across structures small enough to challenge ordinary observation.

00:00:14.342 --> 00:00:18.924
Fast video microscopy captures change over time. The task

00:00:18.924 --> 00:00:23.506
becomes extracting meaningful cardiac and flow measurements from those frames.

00:00:28.300 --> 00:00:33.194
The published work examines cardiac function and blood-flow hemodynamics,

00:00:33.194 --> 00:00:38.088
rather than treating a single attractive frame as quantitative physiology.

00:00:43.175 --> 00:00:47.272
Frame rate, optical scale and analysis assumptions

00:00:47.272 --> 00:00:51.369
can constrain an estimated velocity or physiological parameter.

00:00:55.758 --> 00:00:59.576
Vessels change shape while blood moves. Interpretation has

00:00:59.576 --> 00:01:03.393
to respect both the organism and the measurement technique.

00:01:07.508 --> 00:01:13.179
The 2020 Micron study explores the possibilities of high-speed video

00:01:13.179 --> 00:01:18.849
microscopy. Its original images and analytic details remain the evidence.
